# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Using Qiskit Aer, we were able to simulate this circuit easily. However, "
"suppose we set the number of qubits to 500:\n"
msgstr ""
"Gamit ang Qiskit Aer, madali naming na-simulate ang circuit na ito. "
"Gayunpaman, ipagpalagay na itinakda natin ang bilang ng qubit sa 500:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Because the cost of simulating quantum circuits scales exponentially with "
"the number of qubits, such a large circuit would generally exceed the "
"capabilities of even a high-performance simulator like Qiskit Aer. Classical"
" simulation of generic quantum circuits becomes infeasible when the number "
"of qubits exceeds roughly 50 to 100 qubits. However, note that the "
"efficient_su2 circuit is parameterized by angles on $R_y$ and $R_z$ gates. "
"If all of these angles are contained in the set $\\{0, \\frac{\\pi}{2}, "
"\\pi, \\frac{3\\pi}{2}\\}$, then the circuit is a stabilizer circuit, and it"
" can be efficiently simulated!\n"
msgstr ""
"Dahil ang gastos ng pag-simulate ng mga quantum circuit ay lumalaki nang "
"exponential kasabay ng bilang ng mga qubit, ang ganitong malaking circuit ay"
" karaniwang lalampas sa kakayahan ng kahit isang high-performance simulator "
"tulad ng Qiskit Aer. Ang klasikal na simulation ng mga generic na quantum "
"circuit ay nagiging hindi magagawa kapag ang bilang ng mga qubit ay lumampas"
" sa humigit-kumulang 50 hanggang 100 qubit. Gayunpaman, tandaan na ang "
"efficient_su2 circuit ay parameterized ng mga anggulo sa mga $R_y$ at $R_z$ "
"gate. Kung lahat ng mga anggulong ito ay nasa loob ng set na $\\{0, "
"\\frac{\\pi}{2}, \\pi, \\frac{3\\pi}{2}\\}$, kung gayon ang circuit ay isang"
" stabilizer circuit, at maaari itong mahusay na i-simulate!\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the following cell, we run the circuit with the Sampler primitive backed "
"by the stabilizer circuit simulator, using parameters chosen randomly such "
"that the circuit is guaranteed to be a stabilizer circuit.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa sumusunod na cell, pinapatakbo namin ang circuit gamit ang Sampler "
"primitive na sinusuportahan ng stabilizer circuit simulator, gamit ang mga "
"parameter na pinili nang random upang matiyak na ang circuit ay isang "
"stabilizer circuit.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The stabilizer circuit simulator also supports noisy simulation, but only "
"for a restricted class of noise models. Specifically, any quantum noise must"
" be characterized by a [Pauli "
"error](https://qiskit.org/ecosystem/aer/stubs/qiskit_aer.noise.pauli_error.html#qiskit_aer.noise.pauli_error)"
" channel. [Depolarizing "
"error](https://qiskit.org/ecosystem/aer/stubs/qiskit_aer.noise.depolarizing_error.html)"
" falls into this category, so it can be simulated too. Classical noise "
"channels like [readout "
"error](https://qiskit.org/ecosystem/aer/stubs/qiskit_aer.noise.ReadoutError.html)"
" can also be simulated.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sinusuportahan din ng stabilizer circuit simulator ang noisy simulation, "
"ngunit para lamang sa isang limitadong klase ng mga noise model. Partikular,"
" ang anumang quantum noise ay dapat na nailalarawan ng isang [Pauli "
"error](https://qiskit.org/ecosystem/aer/stubs/qiskit_aer.noise.pauli_error.html#qiskit_aer.noise.pauli_error)"
" channel. Ang [Depolarizing "
"error](https://qiskit.org/ecosystem/aer/stubs/qiskit_aer.noise.depolarizing_error.html)"
" ay nasa kategoryang ito, kaya maaari rin itong i-simulate. Ang mga klasikal"
" na noise channel tulad ng [readout "
"error](https://qiskit.org/ecosystem/aer/stubs/qiskit_aer.noise.ReadoutError.html)"
" ay maaari ring i-simulate.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The following code cell runs the same simulation as before, but this time "
"specifying a noise model that adds depolarizing error of 2% to each CX gate,"
" as well as readout error that flips each measured bit with 5% "
"probability.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang sumusunod na code cell ay nagpapatakbo ng parehong simulation tulad ng "
"dati, ngunit sa pagkakataong ito ay tinutukoy ang isang noise model na "
"nagdaragdag ng depolarizing error na 2% sa bawat CX gate, pati na rin ang "
"readout error na nagbabaliktad ng bawat nasukat na bit na may posibilidad na"
" 5%.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now, let's use the Estimator primitive backed by the stabilizer simulator to"
" compute the expectation value of the observable $ZZ \\cdots Z$. Due to the "
"special structure of stabilizer circuits, the result is very likely to be "
"0.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ngayon, gamitin natin ang Estimator primitive na sinusuportahan ng "
"stabilizer simulator para kalkulahin ang inaasahang halaga ng observable na "
"$ZZ \\cdots Z$. Dahil sa espesyal na istraktura ng mga stabilizer circuit, "
"ang resulta ay malamang na 0.\n"

